            "cites": [2]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Her campaign says she led efforts to expand Medicaid to 800,000 uninsured Illinois residents. She authored House Bill 40, protecting state abortion rights before Roe v. Wade was overturned. She supported a law allowing adult adoptees access to their original birth certificates. Her campaign states she authored a law requiring insurance to cover contraception and cancer screenings. In 2025, she sponsored a bill for student mental health screenings starting in third grade. She also sponsored the 2023 Electric Vehicle Charging Act.",
